Over the last year, I’ve been building something called:

![](/img/overwatch-os-alpha-qa.png)

# Overwatch OS — A Probabilistic Decision Operating System

At first, the project focused on sports analytics, decision tracking, and risk management.

But over time, I realized something important:

> Sports betting was never really the product.

It was simply the first testing environment.

The bigger idea behind Overwatch OS is much broader.

---

## The Problem

Today, we live in a world with:

* artificial intelligence
* real-time data
* powerful computers
* cloud systems
* automation
* global communication

Yet many important systems still struggle with major problems.

We still deal with:

* confusing tax systems
* expensive healthcare
* slow infrastructure projects
* disconnected government systems
* inefficient workflows
* poor incentives
* wasted resources
* bad communication between systems

The more I studied these problems, the more I noticed something:

> Many modern problems are not technology problems.

They are systems problems.

---

## Thinking Like a Systems Engineer

Most large systems work in similar ways.

Whether you look at:

* finance
* transportation
* healthcare
* infrastructure
* logistics
* construction
* economics
* public policy

…you still see the same things:

* uncertainty
* incentives
* risk
* feedback loops
* human behavior
* resource allocation
* operational inefficiency

That realization changed the direction of Overwatch OS.

[Sample Taxation Proposal](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SK0zvFBjBZhK4OCZg91Lh0MQdCckqPa3/view?usp=sharing)

